  + initial formation signature bound the current source-custody evidence manifest even though that manifest intentionally tracks mutable parent navigation
  + the governed recursive rehasher refreshed that manifest after parent formation navigation changed and both formation verifiers refused the stale signature binding

& [Impact]
  + no source canonical requirement or capability semantic changed and no publication occurred
  + the attempted 24-artifact 23-binding inner formation set was structurally unstable

& [Recovery]
  + exclude the transitive current source-custody manifest from the immutable signature and formation inner set
  + retain source document manifest custody proof publication proof and exact source identity in the signature while retaining the current manifest in outer recursive evidence
  + corrected inner set is 23 artifacts with 22 signature bindings and reruns all canonical adversarial dual-PowerShell gates

& [Lesson]
  + signed inner formation sets may bind immutable predecessor artifacts but not a current recursive manifest whose purpose is to follow mutable navigation

